c(55, "§6.6 trial experiment table", "anti-pattern", "The trial natural experiment (before 24 Jan 2026 n = 986 vs after n = 246): hard paywall 17.24% → 34.96% (+17.72pp); onboarding before price 11.87% → 15.85%; advertised as free 2.13% → 6.50%; no free trial 7.00% → 8.54%; trial charged immediately 0 → 11 (4.47%); trial used 0.20% → 2.85%; mean 2.77 → 2.78 — the trial did not solve the problem it was introduced to solve; it requires a card and charges at once or at expiry without effective warning: 'I signed up for the 1 week free trial and was immediately charged AU$17.98'; 'immediately charged for one year. It does not show up in your Apple subscriptions and there is no way to cancel your trial!'; cancelled a day early and still charged $50; 'They made a loop so you can not use the app if you don't accept the free trial'; a 7-day trial only on the annual plan billed €14.99 immediately — causation not established (concurrent ads, 246 reviews) but consistent across four themes: 'a card-gated auto-charging trial with an unclear exit has the reputational cost of a paywall plus the reputational cost of a billing surprise'", "card-gated auto-charging trial, annual-only, forced loop", "billing surprise added to paywall anger", "B01 +17.72pp; 11 charged", "negative", "medium-high", "general", ["13668928014","13887104942","13991693711","13996564291","14031955343","14203716713","14303233696","14309471713","14413359762","14504421154","14508328179"])
